# Calibrate Error Messages

## Step

Decide whether a judged question about error messages after an empty form submit (WCAG 2.1 3.3.1 Error Identification, 3.3.3 Error Suggestion) can ship, by the decision 29 bar: at least 30 real items labelled by hand before the answers are seen, one recorded Clef run, precision at least 0.9 on items the threshold was not chosen on. Until then no such question is in `JUDGED_CHECKS`, so nothing is asked or shown.

## Where things are (2026-11-04)

- Evidence: `emptySubmits` in the rendered evidence (`RenderedEvidenceSchema`, `packages/core/src/rendered-evidence.ts`; how the submits send nothing in `docs/rendered-probes.md`). Each submission has `blocked`, `blockedCount`, `left`, and `errors` and `submitted`, which can be null. `errors` holds every invalid field (label, the browser's own message, `aria-invalid`, its description) and up to 10 texts that appeared after the submit (in the form or not, in a live region or not).
- The form run: builder-cloud scans 30 contact, newsletter and registration pages on stage dev, one at a time, with the submit fix verified (5f01dff). The URL list is `dev-form-urls.txt` in builder-judge's 2026-11-04 scratchpad; progress is in builder-cloud's `form-run/scans.tsv` (15 of 30 done at the time of writing). Each scan archives its evidence in dev's R2 bucket at `<slug>/<scanId>.rendered-evidence.json`; the slug and scan ID are columns 2 and 3 of `scans.tsv`.
- Labelled: nothing yet. The evidence is not in hand.
- Search forms and forms with a password or payment field are never submitted, and only the first three forms per page are, so expect fewer than 30 submissions from 30 pages.

## Next run

1. Collect the 30 archived evidence files from R2 into a fixture folder, keeping only `emptySubmits`.
2. Per submission that was blocked or showed errors, write down by hand, before any model answer: does the page say in text which field is wrong (3.3.1), and does it say how to fix it (3.3.3)? Leave a submission unscored where a person cannot tell from the evidence. A field that only has the browser's own message is identified by the browser, so label it on what the site added.
3. If fewer than 30 submissions are scorable, add contact pages from the round 3 language-hunt hosts and ask builder-cloud for a second dev run. Do not submit forms from a local browser: only the Browser Run session has the guards that make a submit send nothing.
4. Draft the question in `packages/core/src/judged.ts` hidden, split the submissions by site into two halves, pick the threshold on one and report precision on the other.

## Tokens

About 20,000: up to 3 submissions per page with up to 10 messages and 40 fields each, so about 600 tokens a page. That fits one day's calibrator share (`CALIBRATION_JUDGE_TOKENS`, 100,000 by default) with room for a second run.
